00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:19,760
Language takeaway.

58
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:25,860
Okay, so this first word is a very important word in banking and finance.

59
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:28,200
We talk about portfolios a lot.

60
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:28,980
So portfolio.

61
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:29,860
Right.

62
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:35,400
So basically a portfolio is the variety of things that you own.

63
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:40,780
For example, in the stock market, it could be stocks, it could be bonds, it can be mutual funds, etc.

64
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:47,160
Or for example, if you're a company, your product portfolio could be all the products that your company owns.

65
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:47,540
That's right.

66
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:51,960
So in this case, our portfolio is worth half what it was a week ago.

67
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:57,140
And so this is a sentence that means, we've lost half of the money we invested.

68
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:59,220
All of our investments are in a portfolio.

69
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,380
We talk about them as a portfolio.

70
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:05,980
And when we lose money, we say our portfolio is worth less now than it was before.

71
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:06,340
Exactly.

72
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:13,040
So moving on, he starts to talk about the bull market and the bear market.

73
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,480
So what is this all about?

74
00:04:14,790 --> 00:04:16,870
Well, a bull is an animal with horns.

75
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,480
And a bear is another animal.

76
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,840
So we're not talking about animals here.

77
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:25,040
We're talking about special finance phrases.

78
00:04:25,050 --> 00:04:29,610
So the bull market would be, again, talking about companies and trading.

79
00:04:30,310 --> 00:04:32,790
It would be maybe a market that's growing very rapidly.

80
00:04:33,110 --> 00:04:34,090
That's very, very strong.

81
00:04:34,310 --> 00:04:35,190
That's a bull market.

82
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:38,560
So people often talk about China's bull market, right?

83
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:41,920
How China continues to grow and grow and grow and grow.

84
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:45,920
But a market that slows down, like the United States last year, would be a bear market.

85
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:46,280
Right.

86
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:50,480
So think of a bear, maybe it's sleeping, it goes into hibernation.

87
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:51,960
That's a bear market.

88
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,680
So a slow market.

89
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,200
It's not really growing.

90
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:55,440
Very good.

91
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:58,190
But talking about a portfolio again, we might have stocks.

92
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:01,530
But in this case, the two people are talking about their bonds.

93
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:06,600
So he says, you still have some high yield trash bonds and government bonds.

94
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:09,010
What's a high yield bond and what's a trash bond?

95
00:05:09,290 --> 00:05:09,590
Okay.

96
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:13,730
So when we think about the word yield is how much it gives, right?

97
00:05:14,150 --> 00:05:15,690
So how much we are getting from it.

98
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:19,890
So something that is high yield means that you're getting a lot from it.

99
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:25,080
For example, this orange tree yields 300 oranges per year.

100
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,360
Okay.

101
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,360
So how much we get from it.

102
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,360
Exactly.

103
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,360
So we're getting 300 oranges.

104
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:30,060
That's how much it's yielding.

105
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:34,320
And so basically that's what yield means.

106
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:48,100
So when we talk about trash bonds, this on the other hand, it's a word that's maybe a little bit tricky, but a bond is a promise that you get from the seller that he's going to pay you back the money that you give him with interest.

107
00:05:49,050 --> 00:05:51,770
But a trash bond is a very risky bond.

108
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:57,600
It means that the seller might not pay you back because he's still trying to get all the money.

109
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:05,880
Right, but a high yield trash bond means that you might make a lot of money from this bond unless of course it's not very dependable.

110
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:06,390
Exactly.

111
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:07,920
So it's risky.

112
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:10,050
Of course, since it's riskier, it has more yield.

113
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,720
Great.

114
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,810
So high yields trash bond.

115
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,210
And then what about this?

116
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:17,570
They will give us liquidity to cut our losses.

117
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:18,450
Liquidity.

118
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:21,000
We hear all about liquidity in finance.

119
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:21,210
Exactly.

120
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,720
Maybe in your company, the accountant will talk about this.

121
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:27,850
And that's basically just to have money cash in hand.

122
00:06:28,210 --> 00:06:31,430
So you have money to pay things or to buy things.

123
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,280
Not with...

124
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,280
So it's available.

125
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:34,590
Available, yeah.

126
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:36,280
Not with credit.

127
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:36,730
The opposite of credit.

128
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:39,440
Okay, liquidity.

129
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,840
And finally, instead, what are we going to do?

130
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:42,790
Let's think outside the box.

131
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:47,290
We could reinvest in emerging markets.

132
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:51,370
And this is a very hot topic lately, talking about emerging markets.

133
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:54,760
So to emerge means to come up, to rise.

134
00:06:54,770 --> 00:06:55,390
Yeah, to come out.

135
00:06:55,610 --> 00:06:58,970
So it's almost like new or growing markets.

136
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:10,440
So in this case, a market, an emerging market would be, for example, the Southeast Asian market, which is growing quickly, or even you could say West African market.

137
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:13,140
We're talking about places in the world that aren't established.

138
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,220
They're not old and dependable.

139
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:16,180
They're new and exciting.

140
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:16,660
Right.

141
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:18,640
So they're coming up.

142
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:19,760
So that's an emerging market.

143
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:22,360
So a lot of very interesting words and phrases.

144
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,720
They're very related to our topic.

145
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,080
